                  %a{:href => "#quillens_theorems_a_and_b"} Quillen’s theorems A and B
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called
            %em geometric realization of categories
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            that sends
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(\mathcal{C})
            that is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of the category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert N(\mathcal{C})\vert}
            of this simplical set. Typically one is interested in this geometric realization up to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
          %p
            By the
            = succeed "-theorem" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            of simplicial sets constitutes a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"}> Quillen
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} equivalence
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical homotopy theory of simplicial sets
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical homotopy theory of topological spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(\mathcal{C})
            of a category, with the latter regarded as a model for an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrant+replacement"} Kan fibrant replacement
            of the nerve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(\mathcal{C})
            (which still has the same geometric realization, up to weak homotopy equivalence).
          %p
            Therefore an equivalent perspective on geometric realization of categories is that it universally turns a category into an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"} infinity-groupoid
            by freely turning all its morphisms into
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} homotopy equivalences
          %p Geometric realization of categories has various good properties:
          %p
            It sends
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences+of+categories"} equivalences of categories
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            (corollary
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealizationOfEquivalenceIsHomotopyEquivalence"}
            below). A more general sufficient criterion for the geometric realization of a functor is given by the seminal theorem known as
            %em Quillen’s theorem A
            (theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenTheoremA"}
            below.)
          %p
            The existence of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomason+model+structure"} Thomason model structure
            (
            %a{:href => "#ThomasonModelStructure"}> below
            ) implies that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            arises as the geometric realization of some category. In fact it already arises as the geometric realization of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%280%2C1%29-category"}> (0,1)-category
            ).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo →
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  N \colon Cat \to sSet
          %p
            for the
            %a{:href => "nerve#NerveOfACategory"} nerve functor
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo :
                  %mi sSet
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\vert - \vert} : sSet \to Top
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
          %p
            The
            %em geometric realization of categories
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composite
            of these two operations:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ≔
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\vert - \vert} \coloneqq {\vert N(-)\vert} \;\colon\; Cat \to Top
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#ThomasonModelStructure Thomason model structure
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            whose weak equivalences are those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}
            which under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            become weak equivalences in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomason+model+structure"} Thomason model structure
          %p
            The existence of the Thomas model structure implies that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            arises as the geometric realization of some category, in fact already as the realization of some
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%280%2C1%29-category"} (0,1)-category
          #PosetOfSimplicesInNerveOfCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla C
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              of non-degenerate
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplices"} simplices
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subdivision"} subdivision
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N C
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For every category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              the poset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla \mathcal{C}
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PosetOfSimplicesInNerveOfCategory"}
              has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weakly homotopy equivalent
              geometric realization
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ∇
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi wh
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\vert N(\nabla \mathcal{C}) \vert}
                    \\;\simeq_{wh}\;
                    {\vert \mathcal{C} \vert}
                    \\,.
          %p
            (e.g. by
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "Barratt+nerve#BaSdIsHomotopyGood"} this Prop.
          %h3#recognizing_weak_equivalences_quillens_theorem_a_and_b Recognizing weak equivalences: Quillen’s theorem A and B
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}, \mathcal{D}
            be two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            and let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F \;\colon\; \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}
          %p
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            between them.
          #QuillenTheoremA.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "#Quillen72"}> Quillen 72
                , theorem A)
            %p
              If for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathcal{D}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert N(F/d)\vert}
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F/d
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
              (meaning that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a “homotopy
              = succeed "\u201D," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofinal+functor"} cofinal functor
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofinal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} cofinal (∞,1)-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒟
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\vert N(F) \vert}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    {\vert N(\mathcal{C}) \vert}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    {\vert N(\mathcal{D}) \vert}
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
          #QuillenTheoremB.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "#Quillen72"} Quillen 72
                theorem B)
            %p
              If for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \mathcal{D}
              we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert N(F/d)\vert}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weakly homotopy equivalent
              to a given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and all morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon d_1 \to d_2
              induce
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
              between these, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              of
