            %a{:href => "#Arakawa24"}> Arakawa24, Proposition 2.26
            ) and (
            %a{:href => "#KSW24"}> KSW24, Lemma A.1
            ). More discussions can be found in (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski19"}> Cisinski19, Section 4.6
            ).
          %h3#natural_transformations_and_homotopies Natural transformations and homotopies
          #NaturalTrafoMapsToHomotopy.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta : F \Rightarrow G
              between two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F, G : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}
              induces under geometric realization a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {|N(\eta)|} \colon {\vert N(F)\vert} \longrightarrow {\vert N(G) \vert}
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p The natural transformation is equivalently a functor of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta \;\colon\; \mathcal{C} \times \{0 \to 1\} \to \mathcal{D}
            %p
              out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+category"} product category
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              with the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+category"} interval category
            %p
              Since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              preserves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+products"} Cartesian products
              (see there) we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi iso
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\vert N( \mathcal{C} \times \{0,1\} ) \vert}
                    \\;\simeq_{iso}\;
                    {\vert N(\mathcal{C}) \vert} \times {\vert N(\{0 \to 1\}) \vert}
            %p
              But this is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+object"} cylinder object
              in topological spaces, hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert N(\eta) \vert}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+homotopy"} left homotopy
          #RealizationOfEquivalenceIsHomotopyEquivalence.num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \simeq \mathcal{D}
              induces a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              between their geometric realizations.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The statement still remains true for a pair of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ⇆
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \leftrightarrows \mathcal{D}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Notice that the converse is far from true: Very different categories can have geometric realizations that are (weakly) homotopy equivalent. This is because geometric realization implicitly involves
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrant+replacement"} Kan fibrant replacement
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} equivalences
          #RealizationWithTerminalObjectIsContractible.num_cor
            %h6#corollary_2 Corollary
            %p
              If a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              has an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              or a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Assume the case of a terminal object, the other case works
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formally dually
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
              for the terminal category.
            %p Then we have an equality of functors
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ⊥
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Id_* = (* \stackrel{\bottom}{\to} C \to *)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the first functor on the right picks the terminal object, and we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi C
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ⊥
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Id_C \Rightarrow (C \to * \stackrel{\bottom}{\to} C)
            %p whose components are the unique morphisms into the terminal object.
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NaturalTrafoMapsToHomotopy"}
              it follows that we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo =
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert N(\mathcal{C}) \vert \to \vert N(\ast) \vert = \ast
          %h3#behaviour_under_homotopy_colimits Behaviour under homotopy colimits
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon \mathcal{D} \to Cat
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi F
                    %mi Cat
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\vert N(F(-))\vert}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\mathcal{D}
                    \\overset{F}{\longrightarrow}
                    Cat
                    \\stackrel{\vert N(-) \vert}{\to}
                    Top
            %p be its postcomposition with geometric realization of categories
            %p
              Then we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mi N
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi F
                        %mo )
                      %mo |
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi hocolim
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\left\vert N\left(\int F \right) \right\vert}
                    \\simeq
                    hocolim {\vert N(F(-)) \vert}
            %p
              exhibiting the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vert N(F (-)) \vert
              as the geometric realization of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int F
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Thomason79"}> Thomason 79
            ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
              %ul
                %li
                  %strong> of categories
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+simplicial+topological+spaces"} of simplicial topological spaces
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+cohesive+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} of cohesive ∞-groupoids
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            For general references see also
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
          %h3#quillens_theorems_a_and_b Quillen’s theorems A and B
          %p The original articles are
          %ul
            %li#McCord66
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+C.+McCord"}> Michael C. McCord
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Singular homology groups and homotopy groups of finite topological spaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/mccord1.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Quillen72
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
                ,
                %em Higher algebraic K-theory, I: Higher K-theories
                Lect. Notes in Math. 341 (1972), 85-1 (
                %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/~hrm/kansem/quillen-higher-algebraic-k-theory.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Quillen78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy properties of the poset of nontrivial p-subgroups of a group
          %p
            The geometric realization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+constructions"} Grothendieck constructions
            has been analyzed in
          %ul
            %li#Thomason79
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/R.+W.+Thomason"}> R. W. Thomason
              ,
              %em Homotopy colimits in the category of small categories
              , Math. Proc. Cambridge Philos. Soc. 85 (1979), no. 1, 91109.(
              %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/32ACB453B263410CE1643E682D7DE335/S0305004100055535a.pdf/homotopy-colimits-in-the-category-of-small-categories.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p Review is in
          %ul
            %li#Barmak10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Barmak"}> Jonathan Barmak
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em On Quillen’s Theorem A for posets
              %p
                Pages 2445-2453 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1005.0538"}> arXiv:1005.0538
                )
          %p Further development includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clark+Barwick"}> Clark Barwick
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Kan"} Daniel Kan
                %em
                  A Quillen theorem
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_n
                  for homotopy pullbacks
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1101.4879"}> arXiv:1101.4879
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Roberts"}> David Roberts
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy types of topological stacks of categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://nyjm.albany.edu/j/2024/30-41.html"} journal version
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.02778"} arXiv:2204.02778
          %p
            For variations of Quillens’ Theorem B and its generalizations for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} (infinity,1)-categories
          %ul
            %li#LM15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zhen+Lin+Low"}> Zhen Lin Low
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Mazel-Gee"} Aaron Mazel-Gee
                = succeed "," do
                  %em From fractions to complete Segal spaces
                %strong 17
                1 (2015) 321–338 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.8192"}> arXiv:1409.8192
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4310/HHA.2015.v17.n1.a16"} doi:10.4310/HHA.2015.v17.n1.a16
            %li#Cisinski19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
                , Section 4.6 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher categories and homotopical algebra
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://cisinski.app.uni-regensburg.de/CatLR.pdf"} available at the author’s webpage
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781108588737"} doi:10.1017/9781108588737
            %li#Arakawa24
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kensuke+Arakawa"}> Kensuke Arakawa
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Context for Manifold Calculus
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.03321"} arXiv:2403.03321
            %li#KSW24
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord>
                  Eilind Karlsson
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Eilind+Karlsson"} ?
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudia+Scheimbauer"} Claudia Scheimbauer
                = succeed "," do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    Tashi Walde
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Tashi+Walde"} ?
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Assembly of Constructible Factorization Algeras
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.19472"} arXiv:2403.19472
